Guo et al. selected Pak choi (Brassica rapa L. ssp. chinensis) as a
representative leafy vegetable to be tested in pots to reveal the effects
of silicate–phosphate amendments on soil Cd chemical fractions,
total plant Cd levels, and plant bioaccessibility. The authors
used three heavy metal-immobilizing agents, namely wollastonite,
